-- Stormwind City. Donna (entry 2532, guid 20079721) and William (entry 2533, guid 20079720),
-- the two kids who chase each other around the city, had MovementType=2 on their spawns but no
-- waypoint path and no creature_addon PathId, so both stood at their spawn points all day.
-- Donna gets the vanilla 77-node chase loop (cMaNGOS classic-db creature_movement_template for
-- entry 2533 - the same loop the post-Cataclysm role-reversed pair still runs: Trade District
-- streets plus the canal walkway at the borders of Cathedral Square, Old Town and the Dwarven
-- District) and William trails 3.5 yd behind her through creature_formations (groupAI 512 =
-- FLAG_IDLE_IN_FORMATION; without it the leader never tells the member to move), matching this
-- world's role-reversed dialogue (Donna has the Grindgear Gorilla, William wants it back).
-- NB: LeaderStartedMoving() adds PI to the stored angle before the formation generator sees it,
-- so angle=0 means "directly behind the leader" - do not "fix" this to 180. The leader also
-- needs its own self-row in creature_formations or FormationMgr strips the whole formation.
-- Safe to run again.
DELETE FROM `waypoint_path_node` WHERE `PathId`=800797210;
DELETE FROM `waypoint_path` WHERE `PathId`=800797210;
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `PathId`=VALUES(`PathId`);
DELETE FROM `creature_formations` WHERE `memberGUID` IN (20079720,20079721);
UPDATE `creature` SET `MovementType`=0 WHERE `guid`=20079720;
